Subject: [PATCH] mm/page_alloc: accept no memory ahead of use before the watermarks are set

get_page_from_freelist() and alloc_pages_bulk() call cond_accept_memory()
for every allocation, before they look at the watermark, to keep accepted
free memory at the promo watermark. Until init_per_zone_wmark_min() has
run, a postcore initcall, that watermark is zero, and cond_accept_memory()
then accepts one MAX_ORDER block per call "to ensure progress". Early boot
makes hundreds of allocations before the initcall, so a guest with lazy
acceptance accepts a block for each of them, out of whatever its firmware
left unaccepted, before it has used any of it: boot time, and memory its
host has to back for as long as the guest lives.

The proactive calls now do nothing until the watermarks are set. The calls
that follow a failed watermark check or an empty free list are unchanged,
and they are the ones that ensure progress: an allocation that finds no
accepted memory still accepts a block.

Linux-Version: 6.18.49
---
--- a/mm/page_alloc.c
+++ b/mm/page_alloc.c
@@ -319,6 +319,21 @@
 static bool page_contains_unaccepted(struct page *page, unsigned int order);
 static bool cond_accept_memory(struct zone *zone, unsigned int order,
 			       int alloc_flags);
+
+/*
+ * Keep accepted memory ahead of the allocator. This runs for every
+ * allocation, before the watermark is looked at. Until the watermarks are
+ * set there is nothing to keep ahead of, and cond_accept_memory() would
+ * accept a block on every call: a zone's worth of memory in early boot, a
+ * block for each allocation. An allocation that finds no accepted memory
+ * still gets its block, from the callers that act on the result.
+ */
+static void accept_memory_ahead(struct zone *zone, unsigned int order,
+				int alloc_flags)
+{
+	if (promo_wmark_pages(zone))
+		cond_accept_memory(zone, order, alloc_flags);
+}
 static bool __free_unaccepted(struct page *page);
 
 int page_group_by_mobility_disabled __read_mostly;
@@ -3854,7 +3869,7 @@
 			continue;
 		}
 
-		cond_accept_memory(zone, order, alloc_flags);
+		accept_memory_ahead(zone, order, alloc_flags);
 
 		/*
 		 * Detect whether the number of free pages is below high
@@ -5118,7 +5133,7 @@
 			goto failed;
 		}
 
-		cond_accept_memory(zone, 0, alloc_flags);
+		accept_memory_ahead(zone, 0, alloc_flags);
 retry_this_zone:
 		mark = wmark_pages(zone, alloc_flags & ALLOC_WMARK_MASK) + nr_pages;
 		if (zone_watermark_fast(zone, 0,  mark,
